# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[ffsim](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/) is a high-performance simulator for fermionic quantum circuits that exploits particle number and spin-Z conservation to represent state vectors more compactly than a generic $2^n$-dimensional qubit statevector. It defines protocols that any object can implement to participate in its simulation machinery (see [`qiskit_fermions.protocols`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/protocols#module-qiskit_fermions.protocols \"qiskit_fermions.protocols\") for this package’s own protocols, which follow the same design):\n"
msgstr "[ffsim](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/) este un simulator de înaltă performanță pentru circuite cuantice fermionice, care exploatează conservarea numărului de particule și a spinului Z pentru a reprezenta vectorii de stare mai compact decât un vector de stare generic pe qubiți de dimensiune $2^n$. Definește protocoale pe care orice obiect le poate implementa pentru a participa la mecanismul său de simulare (vezi [`qiskit_fermions.protocols`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/protocols#module-qiskit_fermions.protocols \"qiskit_fermions.protocols\") pentru protocoalele proprii ale acestui pachet, care urmează același design):\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[`ffsim.SupportsApplyUnitary`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.SupportsApplyUnitary.html#ffsim.SupportsApplyUnitary \"(in ffsim)\"), by the method `_apply_unitary_(vec, norb, nelec, copy)`, applying the object as a unitary to a fixed-particle-number state vector\n"
msgstr "[`ffsim.SupportsApplyUnitary`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.SupportsApplyUnitary.html#ffsim.SupportsApplyUnitary \"(in ffsim)\"), prin metoda `_apply_unitary_(vec, norb, nelec, copy)`, care aplică obiectul ca unitar unui vector de stare cu număr fix de particule\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[`ffsim.SupportsLinearOperator`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.SupportsLinearOperator.html#ffsim.SupportsLinearOperator \"(in ffsim)\"), by the method `_linear_operator_(norb, nelec)`, returning a [`scipy.sparse.linalg.LinearOperator`](https://docs.scipy.org/doc/scipy/reference/generated/scipy.sparse.linalg.LinearOperator.html#scipy.sparse.linalg.LinearOperator \"(in SciPy v1.18.0)\") view of the object on that same sector\n"
msgstr "[`ffsim.SupportsLinearOperator`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.SupportsLinearOperator.html#ffsim.SupportsLinearOperator \"(in ffsim)\"), prin metoda `_linear_operator_(norb, nelec)`, care returnează o vedere [`scipy.sparse.linalg.LinearOperator`](https://docs.scipy.org/doc/scipy/reference/generated/scipy.sparse.linalg.LinearOperator.html#scipy.sparse.linalg.LinearOperator \"(in SciPy v1.18.0)\") a obiectului în același sector\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[`ffsim.SupportsTrace`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.SupportsTrace.html#ffsim.SupportsTrace \"(in ffsim)\"), by the method `_trace_(norb, nelec)`, returning the object’s trace on that sector.\n"
msgstr "[`ffsim.SupportsTrace`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.SupportsTrace.html#ffsim.SupportsTrace \"(in ffsim)\"), prin metoda `_trace_(norb, nelec)`, care returnează urma obiectului în acel sector.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This package implements that interface: every fermionic gate in [`qiskit_fermions.circuit.library`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library#module-qiskit_fermions.circuit.library \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library\") provides `_apply_unitary_`, and [`FermionOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-fermion-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator\") provides `_linear_operator_` and `_trace_`. That is what makes this package’s operators and circuits *compatible* with ffsim, so its tools work on them natively, with no conversion step. [`ffsim.apply_unitary()`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.apply_unitary.html#ffsim.apply_unitary \"(in ffsim)\") can simulate a [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") end to end, [`ffsim.linear_operator()`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.linear_operator.html#ffsim.linear_operator \"(in ffsim)\") can diagonalize a [`FermionOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-fermion-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator\"), and sampling utilities like [`ffsim.sample_state_vector()`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.sample_state_vector.html#ffsim.sample_state_vector \"(in ffsim)\") (used in the [SKQD guide](skqd#skqd-getting-started) to turn a simulated statevector into measurement counts) work without modification.\n"
msgstr "Acest pachet implementează acea interfață: fiecare poartă fermionică din [`qiskit_fermions.circuit.library`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library#module-qiskit_fermions.circuit.library \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library\") oferă `_apply_unitary_`, iar [`FermionOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-fermion-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator\") oferă `_linear_operator_` și `_trace_`. Aceasta face operatorii și circuitele acestui pachet *compatibile* cu ffsim, astfel încât instrumentele sale funcționează nativ pe ele, fără niciun pas de conversie. [`ffsim.apply_unitary()`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.apply_unitary.html#ffsim.apply_unitary \"(in ffsim)\") poate simula un [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") de la un capăt la altul, [`ffsim.linear_operator()`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.linear_operator.html#ffsim.linear_operator \"(in ffsim)\") poate diagonaliza un [`FermionOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-fermion-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator\"), iar utilitarele de eșantionare precum [`ffsim.sample_state_vector()`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.sample_state_vector.html#ffsim.sample_state_vector \"(in ffsim)\") (folosit în [ghidul SKQD](skqd#skqd-getting-started) pentru a transforma un vector de stare simulat în numărători de măsurare) funcționează fără modificări.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "What `_linear_operator_` returns is an ordinary SciPy [`LinearOperator`](https://docs.scipy.org/doc/scipy/reference/generated/scipy.sparse.linalg.LinearOperator.html#scipy.sparse.linalg.LinearOperator \"(in SciPy v1.18.0)\"), so [`scipy.sparse.linalg.eigsh()`](https://docs.scipy.org/doc/scipy/reference/generated/scipy.sparse.linalg.eigsh.html#scipy.sparse.linalg.eigsh \"(in SciPy v1.18.0)\") and friends work on it too.\n"
msgstr "Ceea ce returnează `_linear_operator_` este un [`LinearOperator`](https://docs.scipy.org/doc/scipy/reference/generated/scipy.sparse.linalg.LinearOperator.html#scipy.sparse.linalg.LinearOperator \"(in SciPy v1.18.0)\") SciPy obișnuit, deci [`scipy.sparse.linalg.eigsh()`](https://docs.scipy.org/doc/scipy/reference/generated/scipy.sparse.linalg.eigsh.html#scipy.sparse.linalg.eigsh \"(in SciPy v1.18.0)\") și funcțiile similare funcționează și pe el.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Coupling through ffsim’s protocols is what buys this: its actively developed ecosystem of simulation and sampling utilities applies to this package’s circuits and operators unchanged, and users already working with ffsim can mix in this package’s gates and operators without learning another simulation API.\n"
msgstr "Cuplarea prin protocoalele ffsim este ceea ce aduce acest lucru: ecosistemul său de utilitare de simulare și eșantionare, dezvoltat activ, se aplică neschimbat circuitelor și operatorilor acestui pachet, iar utilizatorii care lucrează deja cu ffsim pot amesteca porțile și operatorii acestui pachet fără să învețe un alt API de simulare.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "ffsim is an optional dependency {#ffsim-is-an-optional-dependency}"
msgstr "ffsim este o dependență opțională {#ffsim-is-an-optional-dependency}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "ffsim is declared as an optional extra (`pip install \"qiskit-fermions[ffsim]\"`, or transitively by `[all]`), guarded at runtime by [`HAS_FFSIM`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/utils-optionals#qiskit_fermions.utils.optionals.HAS_FFSIM \"qiskit_fermions.utils.optionals.HAS_FFSIM\") (as was shown above). Installing it unlocks simulation: [`ffsim.SupportsLinearOperator`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.SupportsLinearOperator.html#ffsim.SupportsLinearOperator \"(in ffsim)\") and [`ffsim.SupportsTrace`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.SupportsTrace.html#ffsim.SupportsTrace \"(in ffsim)\") are implemented by converting this package’s [`FermionOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-fermion-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator\") into an [`ffsim.FermionOperator`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.FermionOperator.html#ffsim.FermionOperator \"(in ffsim)\"), so without ffsim they raise [`MissingOptionalLibraryError`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/exceptions#qiskit.exceptions.MissingOptionalLibraryError). Everything that does not simulate (building operators, mapping them, and transpiling the resulting circuits) needs none of it.\n"
msgstr "ffsim este declarat ca extra opțional (`pip install \"qiskit-fermions[ffsim]\"`, sau tranzitiv prin `[all]`), protejat la runtime de [`HAS_FFSIM`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/utils-optionals#qiskit_fermions.utils.optionals.HAS_FFSIM \"qiskit_fermions.utils.optionals.HAS_FFSIM\") (așa cum s-a arătat mai sus). Instalarea lui deblochează simularea: [`ffsim.SupportsLinearOperator`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.SupportsLinearOperator.html#ffsim.SupportsLinearOperator \"(in ffsim)\") și [`ffsim.SupportsTrace`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.SupportsTrace.html#ffsim.SupportsTrace \"(in ffsim)\") sunt implementate prin conversia [`FermionOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-fermion-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator\")-ului acestui pachet într-un [`ffsim.FermionOperator`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.FermionOperator.html#ffsim.FermionOperator \"(in ffsim)\"), deci fără ffsim ele ridică [`MissingOptionalLibraryError`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/exceptions#qiskit.exceptions.MissingOptionalLibraryError). Tot ce nu simulează (construirea operatorilor, maparea lor și transpilarea circuitelor rezultate) nu are nevoie de nimic din toate acestea.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Fermionic simulation lives in a fixed particle-number sector {#fermionic-simulation-lives-in-a-fixed-particle-number-sector}"
msgstr "Simularea fermionică se desfășoară într-un sector cu număr fix de particule {#fermionic-simulation-lives-in-a-fixed-particle-number-sector}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Both `_apply_unitary_` and `_linear_operator_` take an `nelec` argument and represent the state vector over the *fixed-particle-number determinant basis* for that `(norb, nelec)` sector, mirroring ffsim’s (and, transitively, PySCF’s) FCI space setup, rather than the full $2^{\\text{num\\_modes}}$-dimensional space a general qubit simulator would use. This is a much smaller space (its size is a product of binomial coefficients rather than a power of two), but it comes with a hard restriction. Only operators and gates that preserve particle number (and, in the spinful case, each spin species’ particle number individually) can be represented in it. An operator whose action would move amplitude to a different particle number has nowhere to put it.\n"
msgstr "Atât `_apply_unitary_`, cât și `_linear_operator_` primesc un argument `nelec` și reprezintă vectorul de stare peste *baza de determinanți cu număr fix de particule* pentru acel sector `(norb, nelec)`, oglindind configurarea spațiului FCI din ffsim (și, tranzitiv, din PySCF), în loc de spațiul complet de dimensiune $2^{\\text{num\\_modes}}$ pe care l-ar folosi un simulator generic de qubiți. Acesta este un spațiu mult mai mic (dimensiunea lui este un produs de coeficienți binomiali, nu o putere a lui doi), dar vine cu o restricție strictă. Doar operatorii și porțile care păstrează numărul de particule (și, în cazul cu spin, numărul de particule al fiecărei specii de spin individual) pot fi reprezentate în el. Un operator a cărui acțiune ar muta amplitudine către un alt număr de particule nu are unde să o pună.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "ffsim resolves this by rejecting such an operator outright: converting one to a linear operator raises a [`ValueError`](https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/exceptions.html#ValueError) naming which conservation law fails. That is the right default, because applying $\\exp(-i t H)$ for a Hamiltonian $H$ with a non-particle-conserving term would otherwise turn a would-be unitary into a non-unitary, physically-meaningless map.\n"
msgstr "ffsim rezolvă aceasta respingând de-a dreptul un astfel de operator: conversia unuia într-un operator liniar ridică o [`ValueError`](https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/exceptions.html#ValueError) care numește ce lege de conservare eșuează. Aceasta este opțiunea implicită corectă, deoarece aplicarea lui $\\exp(-i t H)$ pentru un Hamiltonian $H$ cu un termen care nu conservă numărul de particule ar transforma altfel o aplicație care ar fi unitară într-una neunitară, fără sens fizic.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") surfaces that rejection from the operator it evolves.\n"
msgstr "[`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") scoate la suprafață acea respingere din operatorul pe care îl evoluează.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") checks that its (embedded) rotation matrix is block-diagonal across the alpha/beta split in the spinful case, and raises a [`ValueError`](https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/exceptions.html#ValueError) if it mixes spin sectors.\n"
msgstr "[`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") verifică dacă matricea sa de rotație (încorporată) este bloc-diagonală pe împărțirea alfa/beta în cazul cu spin și generează o eroare [`ValueError`](https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/exceptions.html#ValueError) dacă aceasta amestecă sectoarele de spin.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Non-particle-preserving simulation is therefore out of reach in fermionic space, by construction of the fixed-sector representation, and that is the price of the compact FCI space which makes fermionic simulation tractable in the first place. If your algorithm needs particle-number-violating operators (for example, a qubit-native error channel, or an operator built for a mapped Hamiltonian that does not conserve particle numbers term by term), transpile to qubits first and simulate the resulting [`QuantumCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit) with a qubit-level simulator instead. Any transpilation route works for this; the [fermionic circuit](circuit#fermionic-circuit-explanation) and [transpilation](transpilation#transpilation-explanation) guides go into more detail, but [`generate_preset_jw_pass_manager()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-presets-generate-preset-jw-pass-manager#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.presets.generate_preset_jw_pass_manager \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.presets.generate_preset_jw_pass_manager\") is a reasonable default choice.\n"
msgstr "Prin urmare, simularea care nu conservă numărul de particule este imposibilă în spațiul fermionic, prin construcția reprezentării cu sector fix, iar acesta este prețul spațiului FCI compact care face simularea fermionică tratabilă încă de la început. Dacă algoritmul tău are nevoie de operatori care încalcă numărul de particule (de exemplu, un canal de eroare nativ pentru qubiți sau un operator construit pentru un Hamiltonian mapat care nu conservă numărul de particule termen cu termen), transpilează mai întâi la qubiți și simulează în schimb [`QuantumCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit) rezultat cu un simulator la nivel de qubit. Orice rută de transpilare funcționează pentru aceasta; ghidurile despre [circuite fermionice](circuit#fermionic-circuit-explanation) și [transpilare](transpilation#transpilation-explanation) oferă mai multe detalii, dar [`generate_preset_jw_pass_manager()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-presets-generate-preset-jw-pass-manager#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.presets.generate_preset_jw_pass_manager \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.presets.generate_preset_jw_pass_manager\") este o alegere implicită rezonabilă.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "The block-spin convention for spinful systems {#the-block-spin-convention-for-spinful-systems}"
msgstr "Convenția block-spin pentru sistemele cu spin {#the-block-spin-convention-for-spinful-systems}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`nelec` is typed `int | tuple[int, int]`, and its type, not a separate flag, is what selects one of the supported mode layouts:\n"
msgstr "`nelec` are tipul `int | tuple[int, int]`, iar tipul său, nu un indicator separat, este cel care selectează unul dintre aranjamentele de moduri acceptate:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "An **int** selects the **spinless** interpretation. The `norb` modes are treated directly as spinless orbitals, and `nelec` is the total particle count.\n"
msgstr "Un **int** selectează interpretarea **fără spin**. Cele `norb` moduri sunt tratate direct ca orbitali fără spin, iar `nelec` este numărul total de particule.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A **pair** `(n_alpha, n_beta)` selects the **spinful** interpretation of `2 * norb` modes under a fixed **block-spin convention**. Modes `0 .. norb` are the alpha (spin-up) orbitals and modes `norb .. 2 * norb` are the beta (spin-down) orbitals. Each spin species is conserved *independently*; an alpha-only term can move an electron between alpha modes but never into a beta mode, and vice versa.\n"
msgstr "O **pereche** `(n_alpha, n_beta)` selectează interpretarea **cu spin** a celor `2 * norb` moduri sub o **convenție block-spin** fixă. Modurile `0 .. norb` sunt orbitalii alfa (spin sus), iar modurile `norb .. 2 * norb` sunt orbitalii beta (spin jos). Fiecare specie de spin este conservată *independent*; un termen doar alfa poate muta un electron între moduri alfa, dar niciodată într-un mod beta, și invers.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This dispatch happens at every ffsim-protocol entry point in this package (gate constructors, `_apply_unitary_placed_` implementations, and the native Rust kernel’s sector compilation), and it is the convention used throughout the [LUCJ](lucj#lucj-transpilation) and [SKQD](skqd#skqd-getting-started) guides (for example, [`InitializeModes.from_hartree_fock()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes.from_hartree_fock \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes.from_hartree_fock\") fills alpha occupations into modes `0 .. n_alpha` and beta occupations into modes `norb .. norb + n_beta`). It is worth contrasting this with the [`qiskit_fermions.operators`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators#module-qiskit_fermions.operators \"qiskit_fermions.operators\") module and [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") in general, which use *generic* mode indices with no inherent spin semantics (see the [fermionic circuit guide](circuit#fermionic-circuit-explanation)). The block-spin meaning is imposed only when a spinful `nelec` is supplied to a simulation call, not baked into the operator or circuit representation itself.\n"
msgstr "Această distribuire are loc în fiecare punct de intrare al protocolului ffsim din acest pachet (constructorii de porți, implementările `_apply_unitary_placed_` și compilarea sectoarelor a nucleului nativ Rust) și este convenția folosită în ghidurile [LUCJ](lucj#lucj-transpilation) și [SKQD](skqd#skqd-getting-started) (de exemplu, [`InitializeModes.from_hartree_fock()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes.from_hartree_fock \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes.from_hartree_fock\") plasează ocupările alfa în modurile `0 .. n_alpha` și ocupările beta în modurile `norb .. norb + n_beta`). Merită comparată cu modulul [`qiskit_fermions.operators`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators#module-qiskit_fermions.operators \"qiskit_fermions.operators\") și cu [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") în general, care folosesc indici de mod *generici*, fără semantică de spin inerentă (vezi [ghidul circuitelor fermionice](circuit#fermionic-circuit-explanation)). Semnificația block-spin este impusă doar atunci când un `nelec` cu spin este furnizat unui apel de simulare, nu este încorporată în reprezentarea operatorului sau a circuitului în sine.\n"

